language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Fill a 9x9 Sudoku grid so that every row, column and 3x3 section holds the digits 1 to 9, keeping the given clues.
given input_grid : matrix indexed by [int(1..9), int(1..9)] of int(0..9)
find grid : matrix indexed by [int(1..9), int(1..9)] of int(1..9)

branching on [grid]

such that
$ the solved grid keeps every digit that is given in the input (0 marks an empty cell)
forAll r, c : int(1..9) . (input_grid[r,c] != 0) -> (grid[r,c] = input_grid[r,c]),
$ each row contains the digits 1 to 9 once each
forAll r : int(1..9) . allDiff([grid[r,c] | c : int(1..9)]),
$ each column contains the digits 1 to 9 once each
forAll c : int(1..9) . allDiff([grid[r,c] | r : int(1..9)]),
$ each 3x3 section contains the digits 1 to 9 once each
forAll bi, bj : int(0..2) . allDiff([grid[3*bi + i, 3*bj + j] | i : int(1..3), j : int(1..3)])
